99 &\equiv -1 \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}
Now we can compute the product modulo 20:
\begin{align*}
77\cdot 88\cdot 99 &\equiv (-3)(8)(-1) \\
&\equiv 24 \\
&\equiv \boxed{4} \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 4

