solution_steps:
To combine the polynomials, we simply add the corresponding coefficients of each term.
\begin{align*}
f(x) &= -3x^2 + x - 4, \\
g(x) &= -5x^2 + 3x - 8, \\
h(x) &= 5x^2 + 5x + 1.
\end{align*}
Adding these polynomials together, we get
\begin{align*}
f(x) + g(x) + h(x) &= (-3x^2 + x - 4) + (-5x^2 + 3x - 8) + (5x^2 + 5x + 1) \\
&= (-3 - 5 + 5)x^2 + (1 + 3 + 5)x + (-4 - 8 + 1) \\
&= \boxed{-3x^2 + 9x - 11}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: -3x^2+9x-11

